{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}\f0\fs24 DocuSign Envelope ID: b2c3d4e5-6f70-4819-a0b1-2c3d4e5f6a7b\par 1. Parties and Recitals\par This Mutual Non-Disclosure Agreement (this "Agreement") is entered into by and between AlphaCorp Holdings, Inc. ("AlphaCorp") and Epsilon Systems, Inc. ("Epsilon"). Each party may disclose information to the other in connection with the Purpose, and each party may act as both a disclosing party ("Discloser") and a receiving party ("Recipient").\par 2. Purpose and Permitted Use\par The "Purpose" is the evaluation of a potential commercial relationship between the parties. Recipient shall use Confidential Information solely for the Purpose and for no other purpose.\par 3. Definition of Confidential Information\par "Confidential Information" means non-public information disclosed by Discloser that is designated as confidential at the time of disclosure or that a reasonable person would understand to be confidential given its nature and the circumstances of disclosure. Information disclosed orally need not be reduced to writing in order to be protected.\par 4. Exclusions from Confidential Information\par Confidential Information does not include information that: (a) was already known to Recipient without a duty of confidentiality; (b) was independently developed by Recipient without reference to or use of Discloser's Confidential Information; (c) is or becomes publicly available through no act or omission of Recipient; or (d) is rightfully received by Recipient from a third party without a duty of confidentiality. Recipient bears the burden of establishing that an exclusion applies.\par 5. Permitted Disclosure to Representatives\par Recipient may disclose Confidential Information only to its employees, affiliates, and professional advisers who need to know it for the Purpose and who are bound by confidentiality obligations no less protective than those in this Agreement ("Representatives"). Recipient remains responsible for any breach by its Representatives.\par 6. Standard of Care\par Recipient shall protect Confidential Information using reasonable care.\par 7. Compelled Disclosure\par If Recipient is required by law or legal process to disclose Confidential Information, it shall, where legally permitted, give Discloser prompt written notice so that Discloser may seek a protective order, and shall disclose only that portion legally required.\par 8. Notice of Unauthorized Disclosure\par Recipient shall notify Discloser promptly upon discovering any unauthorized use, disclosure, or loss of Confidential Information, and shall cooperate reasonably with Discloser to mitigate its effects.\par 9. Term\par This Agreement takes effect on the date of last signature and continues for two (2) years, unless earlier terminated by either party on thirty (30) days written notice. Disclosures may be made only during this period.\par 10. Survival of Confidentiality Obligations\par Recipient's obligations with respect to Confidential Information continue for three (3) years from the date of its disclosure, notwithstanding any expiration or termination of this Agreement.\par 11. Trade Secrets\par With respect to information that constitutes a trade secret under applicable law, Recipient's obligations continue for so long as such information remains a trade secret under applicable law.\par 12. Return or Destruction of Materials\par Upon Discloser's written request, Recipient shall return or destroy all Confidential Information in its possession and, if requested, certify that it has done so. Recipient may retain copies held in routine automated backups and copies it is required to retain by law or legal hold, which remain subject to this Agreement for as long as they are retained.\par 13. No Residual Rights\par Nothing in this Agreement grants Recipient the right to use Confidential Information retained in the unaided memory of its Representatives. Recipient acquires no right to use Confidential Information other than as expressly permitted by this Agreement.\par 14. No License; Ownership\par No license or other right in any patent, copyright, trademark, trade secret, or other intellectual property is granted by this Agreement or by any disclosure made under it. Each party retains all right, title, and interest in its own Confidential Information.\par 15. No Warranty\par All Confidential Information is provided AS IS. Neither party makes any representation or warranty as to the accuracy or completeness of any Confidential Information it discloses.\par 16. Limitation of Liability\par Each party's aggregate liability arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall not exceed fifty thousand dollars ($50,000). This limitation does not apply to a breach of the confidentiality obligations in this Agreement.\par 17. No Obligation to Proceed\par Nothing in this Agreement obligates either party to proceed with any transaction, grants either party exclusivity, or restricts either party from pursuing similar discussions with third parties. Either party may terminate discussions at any time.\par 18. Confidentiality of the Discussions\par Neither party shall disclose the existence or status of the discussions between the parties without the other party's prior written consent, except as required by law or by the rules of a securities exchange.\par 19. Data Protection\par If Confidential Information includes personal data, each party shall handle it in compliance with applicable data protection law. The parties shall enter into a separate data processing agreement before any personal data is disclosed.\par 20. Export Control\par Each party shall comply with applicable export control and sanctions laws with respect to any technical data disclosed under this Agreement.\par 21. Injunctive Relief\par Each party acknowledges that a breach of this Agreement may cause irreparable harm for which monetary damages are an inadequate remedy, and that the non-breaching party is entitled to seek injunctive relief in addition to any other remedy available at law or in equity.\par 22. Governing Law\par This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict of laws principles.\par 23. Dispute Resolution and Venue\par The state and federal courts located in Wilmington, Delaware have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of this Agreement, and each party submits to that jurisdiction.\par 24. Assignment\par Neither party may assign this Agreement without the other party's prior written consent, except to an affiliate or to a successor in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of substantially all of its assets.\par 25. Notices\par Notices under this Agreement must be in writing and sent to the addresses set out beneath the parties' signatures, and are effective on receipt.\par 26. Entire Agreement and Amendment\par This Agreement is the entire agreement between the parties as to its subject matter and supersedes all prior discussions. It may be amended only by a writing signed by both parties.\par 27. Severability\par If any provision of this Agreement is held unenforceable, it shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, and the remaining provisions continue in full force.\par 28. Counterparts\par This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, including by electronic signature, each of which is an original and all of which together constitute one agreement.\par IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.\par AlphaCorp Holdings, Inc.\par By: /s/ Dana Reyes\par Name: Dana Reyes\par Title: Vice President, Legal\par Epsilon Systems, Inc.\par By: /s/ Morgan Ellery\par Name: Morgan Ellery\par Title: General Counsel\par }